  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As effective nuclear charge is 2.60 and valence shell contain 3 electrons so the minimum number of main shells for the given element are two i.e., (n = 2) and its configuration will be  <math><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> .<br/><br/>Hence the given element has 5 electrons in all.<br/><br/>Also, for a neutral atom.<br/><br/>As number of electrons = atomic number  = 5.<br/><br/>Thus, the atomic number of the element is 5.",
    "image": null
  },
